(i) stainless Steel work benches with washable impervious tops; 
(ii) facilities for orderly storage of different potencies and back-potencies of various drugs in an area where air is filtered through 5µ filter; 
(iii) suitable devices for measuring and dispensing of potencies/back-potencies into the potentisation phials; 
(iv) potentiser with counter; 
(v) potentisation shall be done by the method(s) prescribed in the Homoeopathic Pharmacopoeia of 
India; 
(vi) an area of 20 square metres shall be provided for basic installations. 
Note 1 : The requirement of potentiser is not mandatory. The process may be done manually also with proper SOPs. Potentiser, if used, shall be properly validated and shall be calibrated every time before commencement of work for proper performance. 
Note 2 : The manufacturer shall use back-potencies procured from Licensed manufacturers and the firm shall maintain proper records of purchase or shall prepare own back-potencies.

